      "output": "# Key Dash: Music and Chart Module\n\nThis code is a plain browser script with no `export` keyword and no audio files, so it can be pasted into the single HTML file. It is 27 lines long, under the 35-line limit. All top-level declarations become globals that the game code can read: `chart`, `startMusic`, `songTime`, `stopMusic` and the constants. At the top level the code only declares values and builds the `chart` array. Nothing reads the `AudioContext` or starts a timer until a caller invokes `startMusic()`.\n\n```js\nconst BPM=120,SPB=60/BPM,BEATS=90,LOOKAHEAD=0.12,TICK_MS=25;\nconst chart=[];for(let b=8;b<=84;b+=2)chart.push({beat:b,time:b*SPB,type:b%6===0?'bar':'gap'});\nconst MELODY=[0,4,7,12,7,4,2,5,9,12,9,5,4,7,11,14]; // semitones above C4, one note per beat\nlet actx=null,noiseBuf=null,startTime=0,nextStep=0,schedTimer=null;\nfunction startMusic(){ // call from the first click/keydown handler (and again for restart)\n  if(!actx){actx=new (window.AudioContext||window.webkitAudioContext)();\n    noiseBuf=actx.createBuffer(1,Math.floor(actx.sampleRate*0.5),actx.sampleRate);\n    const d=noiseBuf.getChannelData(0);for(let i=0;i<d.length;i++)d[i]=Math.random()*2-1;}\n  actx.resume();if(schedTimer)clearInterval(schedTimer);\n  startTime=actx.currentTime+0.1;nextStep=0;schedule();schedTimer=setInterval(schedule,TICK_MS);return startTime;}\nfunction env(g,t,peak,dur){g.gain.setValueAtTime(peak,t);g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.001,t+dur);}\nfunction tone(type,f0,f1,t,dur,vol){const o=actx.createOscillator(),g=actx.createGain();o.type=type;\n  o.frequency.setValueAtTime(f0,t);if(f1)o.frequency.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(f1,t+dur);\n  env(g,t,vol,dur);o.connect(g).connect(actx.destination);o.start(t);o.stop(t+dur+0.05);}\nfunction noise(t,dur,vol,hp){const s=actx.createBufferSource(),f=actx.createBiquadFilter(),g=actx.createGain();\n  s.buffer=noiseBuf;f.type='highpass';f.frequency.value=hp;env(g,t,vol,dur);\n  s.connect(f).connect(g).connect(actx.destination);s.start(t);s.stop(t+dur+0.05);}\nfunction schedule(){ // lookahead scheduler on the AudioContext clock, eighth-note steps\n  const horizon=actx.currentTime+LOOKAHEAD;\n  while(nextStep<BEATS*2&&startTime+nextStep*SPB/2<horizon){\n    const t=startTime+nextStep*SPB/2,beat=nextStep>>1,off=nextStep&1;\n    noise(t,0.04,off?0.12:0.2,7000); // hi-hat on every eighth\n    if(!off){if(beat%2===0)tone('sine',150,40,t,0.35,0.9); // kick on even beats\n      else{noise(t,0.18,0.5,1500);tone('triangle',200,120,t,0.1,0.3);} // snare on odd beats\n      const f=261.63*Math.pow(2,MELODY[beat%16]/12);tone('triangle',f,0,t,0.45,0.25);tone('sine',f*2,0,t,0.3,0.06);}\n    nextStep++;}\n  if(nextStep>=BEATS*2){clearInterval(schedTimer);schedTimer=null;}}\nfunction songTime(){return actx?Math.max(0,actx.currentTime-startTime):0;}\nfunction stopMusic(){if(schedTimer)clearInterval(schedTimer);schedTimer=null;nextStep=BEATS*2;}\n```\n\n## How it maps to the spec\n\n**Master clock:** All sounds are scheduled at `startTime + step × 0.25 s` on `actx.currentTime`. `setInterval` only wakes the scheduler. Notes are queued up to 0.12 s ahead, so timer jitter does not affect timing.\n\n**`songTime()`** returns 0 in two cases: before `startMusic()` (no context exists yet) and during the 0.1 s lead-in. After that it returns `currentTime − startTime`, which is never below 0. Beat n sounds exactly at `songTime = n × 0.5`.\n\n**Restart:** Calling `startMusic()` again reuses the existing `AudioContext` and sets a new `startTime`. The game's own judgment and score state must be reset by the caller.\n\n**Chart:** There is one entry on every even beat from 8 to 84, which gives 39 obstacles.\n- Beats 0–7 are empty for the warm-up.\n- Obstacles are exactly 2 beats (1 s) apart.\n- Each entry has the shape `{beat, time, type}`.\n- Beats where `beat % 6 === 0` hold a **bar**: 13 bars (12, 18, … 84), cleared by sliding with ↓.\n- All other obstacle beats hold a **gap**: 26 gaps, cleared by jumping with Space/↑.\n\n**Sound:**\n- **Kick:** a sine wave with a pitch drop from 150 to 40 Hz, on even beats.\n- **Snare:** high-passed noise plus a short triangle-wave body, on odd beats.\n- **Hi-hat:** noise high-passed at 7 kHz on every eighth note.\n- **Piano:** a 16-beat C-major phrase played on triangle waves with a sine octave on top.\n\n## Unverified\n- I have not run this code in a browser. No audio output, timing accuracy or sound balance has been checked.\n- If restart is pressed mid-song, sounds already queued in the last 0.12 s will still play once. A brief overlap like this is expected.\n- Safari compatibility through the `webkitAudioContext` fallback has not been tested."
